        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Fetch a complete discussion thread by reference - metadata plus all posts in one call.\n
\n
    Combines search + read + collect: finds the thread by reference, reads metadata\n
    (title, state, contributors), then paginates through all posts returning clean text.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You know a discussion thread\'s reference and want all posts.\n
    - You want thread metadata (contributors, state) alongside post content.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You don\'t know the thread reference - use erp5_search on \'discussion_thread_module\' first.\n
    - You need to read a non-discussion document - use erp5_read or erp5_read_deep instead.\n
    - You only need the thread\'s metadata without posts - use erp5_read.\n
\n
    The reference is the URL-friendly identifier (e.g. \'RFC--moving-to-python3-hiqp60J4cE\'),\n
    not the document title. Find it via erp5_search with select_list=[\'reference\', \'title\'].\n
    </string> </value>
